#: /resources/settings.xml
msgctxt "#32040"
msgid "A quick press. While a game is paused a tap always resumes it, whatever is set here: that is the only way back into a paused game, so it is not a binding. Unavailable while Double tap is set, because every double tap would fire this on its way through."
msgstr ""

#: /resources/settings.xml
msgctxt "#32041"
msgid "Two quick presses. The default opens the on-TV switcher: a list of the running game, Big Picture and the desktop, navigable with the stick."
msgstr ""

#: /resources/settings.xml
msgctxt "#32042"
msgid "Holding the button for the hold time. The default pauses the running game and puts Kodi back on screen. Leave at least one gesture on this: it is the only way out of a game from the couch, and a settings file that binds it away everywhere is rejected and this is put back."
msgstr ""

#: /resources/settings.xml
msgctxt "#32043"
msgid "Fires when the button comes back up after a hold, on top of whatever the hold itself did."
msgstr ""

#: /resources/settings.xml
msgctxt "#32044"
msgid "Holding for the long-hold time. Only available with Hold set to Nothing: the hold fires first and the press is already spent, so with both set the long hold is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: /resources/settings.xml
msgctxt "#32045"
msgid "How long the button must be down to count as a hold rather than a tap. Default 0.9."
msgstr ""

#: /resources/settings.xml
msgctxt "#32046"
msgid "How long after letting go a second press still counts as a double tap. Default 0.35."
msgstr ""

#: /resources/settings.xml
msgctxt "#32047"
msgid "How long the button must be down for a long hold. Must be longer than the hold time. Default 3.0."
msgstr ""
